 Since you’re building a Kafka-based notification service that also fetches user info (via DB or RPC) and
 sends notifications (WhatsApp, email), the best approach would be to go with a Clean Architecture
(a.k.a. Hexagonal Architecture) with clear layering. This gives you Loose coupling between business logic and
external systems.Easy testing and maintenance. Future flexibility (e.g., swap DB or notification provider).



Kafka consumer receives a message.
Passes the message to NotificationService.ProcessTaskCreatedEvent()
NotificationService calls UserRepository.GetUserDetails(watcherIDs)
Once users are fetched, it calls WhatsApp.Send(...) or Email.Send(...)


Pattern	Use
Repository Pattern	For abstracting DB calls (e.g., fetching users)
Service Layer	For business logic (processing events, transforming data)
Factory (optional)	For creating messages or channel-specific payloads

# 📦 Notification Service Directory Layout


📁 notification-service/
├── 📁 cmd/
│   └── 📄 main.go                  # Entry point of the application
├── 📁 config/
│   └── 📄 config.go               # Twilio/API/Env configuration loader
├── 📁 internal/
│   ├── 📁 adapters/               # External tech-specific implementations
│   │   ├── 📁 kafka/
│   │   │   └── 📄 consumer.go     # Kafka consumer implementation
│   │   ├── 📁 notifier/
│   │   │   ├── 📄 email.go        # Email sending logic
│   │   │   └── 📄 whatsapp.go     # WhatsApp sending logic (Twilio)
│   ├── 📁 app/
│   │   └── 📄 notification.go     # Use case orchestration (business logic)
│   ├── 📁 domain/
│   │   ├── 📄 task.go             # TaskMessage entity
│   │   └── 📄 user.go             # UserResponse entity
│   ├── 📁 ports/
│   │   ├── 📄 consumer.go         # Kafka interface
│   │   ├── 📄 sender.go           # Notification interface (email/whatsapp)
│   │   └── 📄 userfetcher.go      # Interface to fetch user (gRPC/DB)
│   ├── 📁 repository/
│   │   ├── 📄 user_pg_repository.go # DB-backed user fetch implementation
│   │   └── 📄 user_repository.go  # Interface for user repository
│   └── 📁 service/
│       └── 📄 notification_service.go # Internal service logic glue layer
├── 📁 proto/
│   └── 📄 (gRPC proto files)       # User service proto definitions
├── 📄 go.mod                       # Go module definition
└── 📄 ReadMe.md5                   # Hash or project info



| Folder                 | Purpose                                              |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `cmd/`                 | Entry point (main app runner)                        |
| `config/`              | Configuration loading (Twilio keys, etc.)            |
| `internal/adapters/`   | External I/O logic (Kafka, Twilio, DB/RPC clients)   |
| `internal/app/`        | Business logic (use cases like "NotifyUser")         |
| `internal/domain/`     | Core models/entities (`TaskMessage`, `UserResponse`) |
| `internal/ports/`      | Interfaces (for DI and testing)                      |
| `internal/repository/` | Repos backed by DBs or gRPC                          |
| `internal/service/`    | Glue logic if needed                                 |
| `proto/`               | gRPC definitions                                     |

